cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mdab: compositional differential abundance methods for 16S data, compared against simulated ground truth"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: ""
    family-names: ""
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A 16S amplicon analysis pipeline that runs ALDEx2 and ANCOM-BC2 on the
  same data, models donor and batch as random effects, screens for
  reagent contaminants with decontam, and evaluates all of it against
  simulated data with known ground truth.
keywords:
  - microbiome
  - 16S rRNA
  - compositional data analysis
  - differential abundance
